Implement user story SKY-004-impl: Implement Express server routes, middleware, and error handling

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts with Express app exporting named `app` separately from a guarded listen() call. Implement GET /health, GET /search, GET /cheapest, GET / (reads src/public/index.html at runtime via fs.readFileSync). Add RAPIDAPI_KEY gating middleware that short-circuits /search and /cheapest with 503 when key absent. Handle SkyscannerClient errors with 500 responses. Import FlightResult from SKY-002. Depends on SKY-002 and SKY-004-dashboard (for src/public/index.html to exist).

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports a named `app` (Express instance) separately from the listen() call so supertest can import it without binding a port
- The listen() call is guarded by `if (import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href)` (ESM) or `if (require.main === module)` (CJS) matching the tsup output format so vitest run never binds a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of whether RAPIDAPI_KEY is set or absent
- GET / returns HTTP 200 text/html with body equal to contents of src/public/index.html read at runtime via fs.readFileSync — hardcoded inline HTML that happens to match is NOT acceptable; this route is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search with valid params (from, to, date; adults optional, defaults 1) returns 200 { flights: FlightResult[], count: flights.length, searchedAt: ISO-8601 }; missing required param (from, to, date) returns 400 { error }; adults non-numeric returns 400 { error }
- GET /cheapest with valid params returns 200 with single cheapest FlightResult (price ≤ all others); missing required params returns 400 { error }; empty SkyscannerClient results returns 404 { error }; adults defaults to 1 if absent
- RAPIDAPI_KEY absent at startup → middleware short-circuits /search and /cheapest with HTTP 503 JSON { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / return normal responses unaffected
- SkyscannerClient throws during /search or /cheapest → server returns HTTP 500 JSON { error: string } without crashing or unhandled rejection; FlightResult type imported from SKY-002 export, not redeclared inline; searchedAt is ISO-8601 distinct per request (≥1ms apart yields different values)





